{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1431223-talking-in-animal-form-what-should-i-charge-v5","id":1431223,"title":"Talking in Animal Form: What should I charge? [V5]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-05T16:05:02-08:00","id":1431223,"title":"Talking in Animal Form: What should I charge? [V5]","content":"I have a gangrel in the chronicle I run who wants to be able to talk in animal form. There are no powers or merits that allow this, but in game they recently ran into a Tzimicie who offer their services to the coterie. The player is thinking since there re no merits maybe the flesh crafter can make a modification to his animal forms.<br /> <br /> I am OK with this. Since it is a relatively minor procedure I didn't want to charge an attribute for it. So I was thinking maybe make a merit to cover it. The question is dot rating. I was thinking 2 dot. Does that sound reasonable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T18:14:19-08:00","id":1431233,"title":"","content":"Dude should have chosen a raven (or parrot) for one of his animal forms and gotten human speech for free!<br /> <br /> As for cost, a 1 dot Merit lets you learn another language, making yourself understood to people who wouldn't have been able to if you didn't share that language. I think that's a good guideline for the amount of utility the modification represents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T19:40:58-08:00","id":1431241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1431223-talking-in-animal-form-what-should-i-charge-v5?p=1431233#post1431233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude should have chosen a raven (or parrot) for one of his animal forms and gotten human speech for free!<br /> <br /> As for cost, a 1 dot Merit lets you learn another language, making yourself understood to people who wouldn't have been able to if you didn't share that language. I think that's a good guideline for the amount of utility the modification represents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T21:26:03-08:00","id":1431251,"title":"","content":"I disagree, learning another language isn't the same as learning to speak entirely. It's certainly not overpowered, but being able to clearly communicate with peers without having to repeatedly burn blood transforming back and forth is a considerable boon. I would say your original feeling of two dots is fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T00:22:55-08:00","id":1431257,"title":"","content":"a 2 point merit seems about right for something a Gangrel could develop. A talking animal isn't going to break the game for 2 points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}